Z||000007||theogre||01-24-2000||08:34 PM||||That's cute. shows how bright they are.....<P>When one looks at the gasket, it looks like it holds the washer. The hole is usually smaller in the gasket. But it's usually not smaller than the manifold port. That, at the least, lets the gasket relax into the manifold. If the washer isn't staked you end up with it leaking wich messes up the EGR metering.<P>If the gasket hole is close to the washer size, the washer can be pulled thru it. That of course can ruin the whole motor.||||reg||1
